          "id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "BUCKLAND SP 81 SE                                              GRAND UNION CANAL                                                       AYLESBURY ARM 5/350                                                 BRIDGE NO 8 II                                                    GV Bridge over canal. 1811-13. Engineer Henry Provis for Grand Junction Canal Company. Red brick, mostly in English bond. Battered plinth. Round arch with number plate over. Raised band below parapet which is rebuilt (late C20) on east side and has chamfered brick coping with end stones. Square projecting end piers on stepped battered plinths terminate the outswept ends of the parapet. The bridge carries a farm track over the canal and has been little altered since the Aylesbury arm opened in 1815. Listing NGR: SP8795013903"
    }
